  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "#### 🐛 Bug Fixes\n\n**I/O**\n- Fixed file size formatting at exact 1000-multiple boundaries\n- Fixed Unix permission notation parsing and stopped counting Deny ACL entries as grants\n- Safely enumeration now includes hidden and system entries and caps recursion depth\n- Aligned Safely enumeration case-sensitivity defaults and returning an empty result for missing directories instead of throwing\n- `GetRandomDrive` now deep-walks candidate drives before declaring that none contain files\n- Guarded drive `HasFiles`/`HasDirectories` against not-ready drives\n- Fixed Linux fallbacks in `GetRandomDirectory` and `DrivesIsEmpty`\n- Fixed a stale `homeTokenIndex` when a PATH entry contains both `~` and `$HOME`\n\n**Numbers**\n- Fixed digit counting for floating point values and infinite generic numeric types\n- Fixed from-end `Index.AsRange` handling, empty incremented-range validation, and truncating behavior in `ToDestinationNumber`\n\n**Strings**\n- Fixed `StringSegment` `Remove` off-by-one errors and a `Contains` throw near the end of the segment\n- Fixed `InsertRange` argument binding and inverted `Remove`-range validation\n- `Insert`/`InsertRange` now accept an append position index equal to `Length`\n- `ReplaceFirst`/`ReplaceLast` now accept an empty replacement value and null-check the receiver\n- Escape character removal is now single-pass and no longer trims edge spaces\n\n**Threading & Security**\n- Fixed `WaitAsync` timeout blocking behavior\n- Fixed `SecureString` validation and wipe bugs\n\n**Dates & Versions**\n- `DateOnly` conversion and week / day-of-week calculations are now culture-safe\n- Fixed inverted XML docs on `Version` comparison predicates",
